  "question": {
    "text": "How many millilitres of <math> <mrow> <mtext>0</mtext><mtext>.5</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>M</mtext></mrow> </math> <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>SO</mtext></mrow> <mtext>4</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> are needed to dissolve <math> <mrow> <mtext>0</mtext><mtext>.5</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>g</mtext></mrow> </math> of copper(II)carbonate?<br />\rReport your answer by rounding it up to nearest integer."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "The balanced chemical reaction is:&nbsp;<br />CuCO<sub>3</sub> + H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub><sub>&nbsp; </sub>→&nbsp; CuS0<sub>4</sub> + H<sub>2</sub>O + CO<sub>2</sub><br />milli mol of CuCO<sub>3</sub> =<math><mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mn>123.5</mn></mfrac></mrow></math><br />= 4.048 mM<br /><math><mrow><mo></mo></mrow></math>milli mol of H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> required = 4.048 mM<br />= Molarity x Volume (in mL)<br /><math><mrow><mo></mo></mrow></math>Volume = <math><mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mn>4.048</mn><mn>0.50</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>= 8.1 mL"
  }
